                "Grain_Size_Value": "1.17 ± 0.29",
                "Grain_Size_Units": "µm",
                "Microstructural_Features": "poor interfacial bonding and increased porosity. Al-Ni-Y-Sc-Co splats have fully amorphous regions and crystalline Al-Ni-Y-Sc-Co splats. High density of LAGBs is concentrated near the splat interiors and boundaries (60.9%). Quantity of (HAGB) is low (39.1%)"
            },
            "Notes": "As-deposited. Secondary powder production method was melting pure elements in a graphite crucible under inert argon atmosphere, then the molten alloy was subjected to high-pressure argon gas atomization. Mean diameter of Al-Ni-Y-Sc-Co powder was 7.8 ± 4.0 µm, and ranged from 2 to 20 µm. Mean diameter of Al 6061 powder was 34.6 ± 13.5 µm, and ranges from 5 to 80 µm. Both powders' size distributions are gaussian. XZ plane shows higher hardness due to anisotropy: 261 ± 8 HV. On splat boundaries the grain size is finer, 1.17 ± 0.29 µm. In the splat centers, grains are coarser, 10.25 ± 5.73 µm. elastic modulus values are also given seperately for the Al-Ni-Y-Sc-Co splats and the Al 6061 regions. The Al-Ni-Y-Sc-Co splats range from 80 to 110 GPa, the Al 6061 regions show a lower modulus range of 65 to 75 GPa."
        },
